.TH GENESIS-REASONING 7 "October 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-reasoning \- the reasoning faculties of the Genesis mind
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBfrontal_lobe.reasoning.reasoner\fR      associative inference over the concept net
\fBfrontal_lobe.reasoning.logic\fR         formal logic: model theory, AGM, Ramsey
\fBfrontal_lobe.reasoning.induction\fR     example-driven rule induction
\fBfrontal_lobe.reasoning.analogy\fR       structure-mapping transfer
\fBfrontal_lobe.reasoning.drift_diffusion\fR  evidence accumulation for decision
\fBparietal_lobe.abstract_reasoning\fR     relational schemas, anti-unification
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Genesis reasons in two deliberately distinct styles \(em the same
fractionation the human literature reports (a left fronto-parietal
system dissociable into propositional, relational, and categorical
subsystems, rather than one unitary "logic").
.PP
The
.B associative
style lives in
.IR reasoner.py :
best-first traversal over the concept network, conclusions held with
confidence, revisable on contradiction. Seven reasoning types
\(em deductive (transitive chains), abductive (best explanation),
analogical, causal, contradiction detection, hypothesis formation,
and synthesis \(em plus belief revision that reweights edge
confidence as evidence arrives. It is fast, semantic, and wrong-
tolerant: what might be true.
.PP
The
.B formal
style lives in
.IR logic.py :
mechanical derivation over sets of sentences \(em what must be true.
Its engine is model enumeration in the spirit of Johnson-Laird's
mental models: a conclusion is valid iff it holds in
.I every
valuation consistent with the premises, and an invalid inference
returns the countermodel that refutes it. The same engine serves
every formal function:
.IP \(bu 2
.B deduction
\(em \fBverify\fR(premises, conclusion) and
.BR entails (kb ", " q)
by refutation;
.IP \(bu 2
.B belief revision
\(em AGM operators over belief sets:
.BR expand (K ", " p),
.BR contract (K ", " p)
(minimal-mutilation removal, least-entrenched first; structural
depth is the default entrenchment \(em literals surrender before
rules), and
.BR revise (K ", " p)
by the Levi identity K*p = (K \(mi ~p) + p;
.IP \(bu 2
.B conditionals and counterfactuals
\(em
.BR ramsey (K ", " p ", " q)
implements the Ramsey test: "if p then q" is acceptable iff K*p
entails q;
.IP \(bu 2
.B abduction
\(em
.BR explain (K ", " q ", " candidates)
returns the smallest consistent subset of candidates entailing the
observation;
.IP \(bu 2
.B categorical deduction
\(em
.BR syllogism (p1 ", " p2 ", " conclusion)
evaluates Aristotelian propositions
.RI ( ALL ", " NO ", " SOME ", " SOME_NOT )
over the 256 Venn-region inhabitance patterns, modern semantics
with no existential import.
.PP
Formulas are small immutable trees
.RI ( Atom ", " not_ ", " and_ ", " or_ ", " implies ", " iff )
with a recursive-descent parser
.RB ( parse
accepts
.IR "a & ~b -> c" ,
unicode connectives, and namespaced atoms like
.IR concept:bird ).
Enumeration is bounded at
.B MAX_ATOMS
(14) \(em 2^14 valuations is instant, and the bound is
intentional: human mental models hold ~3 possibilities, so a problem
too big for the bound is a problem to split, not to brute-force.
.PP
The two styles are complementary organs, not competitors: the
associative reasoner proposes (cheap, fallible, creative); the logic
engine verifies (exact, narrow). Nothing in the associative path is
replaced \(em contradictions found by
.BR consistent ()
feed the existing belief-revision engine, and hypotheses formed
associatively can be confirmed mechanically when the domain admits
formality.
.SH ENTRY POINTS
Each entry: the function, what it takes, and what it returns.
Consumers import from the \fBfrontal_lobe.reasoning\fR package
facade.
.TP
.BR parse (text)
Parse a formula string \(em \fI"a & ~b -> c"\fR, unicode
connectives, namespaced atoms like \fIconcept:bird\fR \(em into an
immutable formula tree.
.TP
.BR models (formulas ", " limit=None)
Enumerate the valuations satisfying the given formulas, bounded by
\fBMAX_ATOMS\fR \(em the witness set a satisfiable theory stands
on.
.TP
.BR satisfiable (formulas)
Ask whether the formulas have any satisfying valuation at all.
.TP
.BR entails (kb ", " q)
Ask whether the knowledge base entails the query \(em true iff the
query holds in every valuation of the premises.
.TP
.BR verify (premises ", " conclusion)
Deduction by refutation: valid iff no valuation satisfies the
premises while falsifying the conclusion \(em an invalid
inference returns the countermodel that refutes it.
.TP
.BR expand (K ", " p)
AGM expansion: add \fIp\fR to the belief set and close.
.TP
.BR contract (K ", " p)
AGM contraction: remove \fIp\fR with minimal mutilation \(em
least-entrenched beliefs surrender first.
.TP
.BR revise (K ", " p)
AGM revision: incorporate \fIp\fR by the Levi identity,
contracting the negation first.
.TP
.BR consistent (K)
Ask whether the belief set is contradiction-free \(em the answer
that feeds belief revision.
.TP
.BR ramsey (K ", " p ", " q)
The Ramsey test for conditionals: "if p then q" is acceptable iff
K revised by p entails q.
.TP
.BR explain (K ", " q ", " candidates)
Minimal abduction: the smallest consistent subset of
\fIcandidates\fR that entails the observation.
.TP
.BR Categorical ", " Quantifier ", " syllogism (p1 ", " p2 ", " conclusion)
Single-step categorical deduction over Aristotelian propositions
(ALL, NO, SOME, SOME_NOT), checked against the 256 Venn-region
inhabitance patterns \(em modern semantics, no existential import.
.TP
.B try_math
The math-question entry point in
.IR reasoning.math_reasoning
(see
.BR genesis-math (7)).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Self_World/frontal_lobe/reasoning/logic.py
The formal engine (pure Python; no solver dependency).
.TP
.I Self_World/frontal_lobe/reasoning/reasoner.py
The associative engine and its seven reasoning types.
.TP
.I Self_World/frontal_lobe/reasoning/
The rest of the package: analogy, belief_revision, blending,
causation, competence, convention, critical_thinking, decision,
foundations, hypotheses, judgment, math_reasoning, method_library,
modal, planning, problem_solving, and theory_of_mind \(em all
exported through the package facade.
.TP
.I Self_World/parietal_lobe/abstract_reasoning.py
Relational schemas and anti-unification (induction over structure).
.TP
.I tests/python/test_logic.py ", " test_reasoning.py
The faculties under test.
.SH GLOSSARY
.TP
.B associative / formal
Her two reasoning styles: the \fIassociative\fR engine proposes
(best-first traversal over the concept network, conclusions held
with revisable confidence \(em what might be true); the \fIformal\fR
engine verifies (mechanical derivation over sentences \(em what
must be true).
.TP
.B model enumeration
The formal engine's method in the spirit of Johnson-Laird's mental
models: a conclusion is valid iff it holds in \fIevery\fR valuation
consistent with the premises; an invalid inference returns the
countermodel that refutes it.
.TP
.B valuation / countermodel
A truth-assignment to the atoms. A countermodel is the valuation
satisfying the premises but not the conclusion \(em the concrete
exhibit of an invalid inference.
.TP
.B AGM
The belief-revision framework for belief sets: \fIexpand\fR adds,
\fIcontract\fR removes minimally (least-entrenched first;
structural depth is the default entrenchment), and \fIrevise\fR
incorporates by the Levi identity K*p = (K \(mi ~p) + p.
.TP
.B entrenchment
How hard a belief is to give up \(em the ordering contraction
respects; literals surrender before rules.
.TP
.B Ramsey test
The conditional's acceptance test: "if p then q" is acceptable
iff the belief set revised by p entails q \(em
.BR ramsey (K ", " p ", " q) .
.TP
.B syllogism
Single-step categorical deduction over Aristotelian propositions
(ALL, NO, SOME, SOME_NOT) evaluated against the 256 Venn-region
inhabitance patterns \(em modern semantics, no existential import.
.TP
.B existential import
The assumption that a universal implies existence ("all S are P"
means an S exists). Her syllogisms use modern semantics: it does
not.
.TP
.B Venn-region inhabitance
The pattern of which regions a categorization populates \(em the
finite model space syllogisms are checked against.
.TP
.B MAX_ATOMS
The enumeration bound (14 atoms, 2^14 valuations) \(em
intentional, matching that human mental models hold ~3
possibilities: a problem too big for the bound is a problem to
split, not to brute-force.
.TP
.B namespaced atom
A formula atom like \fIconcept:bird\fR \(em lets a formal sentence
point into her concept network.
.TP
.B anti-unification
Induction over structure in the parietal lobe \(em finding the
most specific generalization of two relational forms, the way an
analogy's skeleton is extracted.
.TP
.B reasoning types
The associative engine's seven modes: deductive (transitive
chains), abductive (best explanation), analogical, causal,
contradiction detection, hypothesis formation, synthesis.

